To ensure robust and fail-closed behavior, wrap the entire filesystem check and path resolution inside the `try-catch` block in `sha256File`. Currently, `fs.existsSync` is called outside the `try-catch` block, which could throw an unhandled exception if there are permission issues or other I/O failures on certain platforms.

```suggestion
function sha256File(root, relPath) {
  try {
    const target = resolvePath(root, relPath);
    if (!target || !fs.existsSync(target)) return null;
    return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(target)).digest('hex');
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
```

